test:
Don' go roun' a-sayin' hit's a bar'l;
'Ca'se de people gwine to test you, an' dey'll fin' out you's a-lyin',
Den dey'll twis' yo' sayin's in a snarl.

testimony:
On a beggar’s middle finger, and require
More testimony to convict a thief?
A child’s too costly for so mere a wretch;

tested:
And pleasures till he tired of them;
Then, having tested all things, he
Witnessed that all are vanity.

testimonials:
God sent her to his world, commissioned right,
Her human testimonials fully signed,
Not scant in soul—complete in lineaments;
